WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.731 --> 00:00:15.334
the next morning, Heidi awoke to the sound of Grandfather's voice.

2
00:00:15.354 --> 00:00:17.375
"Come along, Heidi!

3
00:00:17.736 --> 00:00:19.577
The sun is up," he said.

4
00:00:19.597 --> 00:00:24.140
"Put on your best dress because we are going to church!"

5
00:00:25.662 --> 00:00:32.101
Heidi was so surprised by her Grandfather's announcement that she dressed quickly with happy anticipation.

6
00:00:33.041 --> 00:00:37.022
When she came down the ladder, she saw a sight she had never seen before.

7
00:00:37.042 --> 00:00:41.283
"Why, Grandfather!"

8
00:00:41.784 --> 00:00:46.305
she exclaimed, "I have never seen you dress so nicely!

9
00:00:47.305 --> 00:00:50.226
Look at your handsome coat and silver buttons!"

10
00:00:51.366 --> 00:00:57.228
He tried not to smile and replied, "I suppose Clara gave you that nice dress.

11
00:00:58.332 --> 00:01:00.313
Well, it makes you look very pretty.

12
00:01:01.274 --> 00:01:03.855
Now come along, we don't want to be late."

13
00:01:05.436 --> 00:01:09.118
They set off hand in hand down the mountain path to the valley below.

14
00:01:10.339 --> 00:01:13.100
The church bells were ringing as they walked through the town.

15
00:01:14.621 --> 00:01:21.325
Inside the church, the townspeople had already taken their seats and the singing had begun when Heidi and

16
00:01:21.385 --> 00:01:22.605
her Grandfather entered.

17
00:01:25.607 --> 00:01:29.305
People turned their heads, and whispers spread from pew to pew.

18
00:01:29.325 --> 00:01:33.027
"Do you see Heidi and her Grandfather?"

19
00:01:33.408 --> 00:01:33.968
they said.

20
00:01:33.988 --> 00:01:35.849
"It can't be!

21
00:01:36.409 --> 00:01:37.650
Grandfather is in church!"

22
00:01:38.891 --> 00:01:44.414
At the end of the service, Grandfather took Heidi's hand, and they walked over to the pastor's house.

23
00:01:46.195 --> 00:01:49.757
The pastor welcomed Heidi and shook hands with Grandfather happily.

24
00:01:50.958 --> 00:01:54.640
"I have come to ask for your help, pastor," said Grandfather.

25
00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:00.762
"I have made up my mind to follow your advice and find a place for us to live

26
00:02:00.822 --> 00:02:02.103
in Dorfli for the winter."

27
00:02:03.683 --> 00:02:05.304
"Wonderful," said the pastor.

28
00:02:05.324 --> 00:02:08.025
"You are always welcome among us!"

29
00:02:09.125 --> 00:02:13.487
The pastor smiled warmly, and they talked about the different houses that were for rent.

30
00:02:14.648 --> 00:02:19.069
Grandfather thanked him for his advice, and they all walked outside to say good-bye.

31
00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:27.549
The townspeople, who had followed Grandfather to the pastor's house, were gathered outside, and the pastor wanted them

32
00:02:27.589 --> 00:02:29.790
to see that Grandfather was always welcome.

33
00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:35.313
"I look forward to spending many pleasant winter evenings together," said the pastor.

34
00:02:37.074 --> 00:02:41.057
Immediately, the people of Dorfli came up to say hello and shake Grandfather's hand.

35
00:02:41.077 --> 00:02:45.339
"We are so pleased to see you both among us!"

36
00:02:45.859 --> 00:02:46.380
some said.

37
00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:51.262
Others exclaimed, "I have been wishing that we could talk together again."

38
00:02:52.963 --> 00:02:57.245
Everywhere he turned, Grandfather was surprised by a friendly welcome.

39
00:02:58.206 --> 00:03:01.008
He had always thought that the people of Dorfli disliked him.

40
00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:07.611
What he didn't know was that Heidi had told the baker, who brought her from the train station,

41
00:03:07.952 --> 00:03:09.512
how much she missed Grandfather.

42
00:03:11.213 --> 00:03:15.016
He had told the whole town what a kind man he was to Heidi.

43
00:03:15.996 --> 00:03:21.479
Grandfather explained that he was going to rent a house for the winter in Dorfli, and everyone was

44
00:03:21.539 --> 00:03:22.640
very happy to hear it.

45
00:03:24.264 --> 00:03:30.146
On the way home, many new and old friends walked part way up the mountain with Grandfather and

46
00:03:30.186 --> 00:03:37.047
Heidi. When they were climbing the path alone again, Heidi noticed the sunlight shining on Grandfather's face.

47
00:03:37.068 --> 00:03:43.729
"Grandfather, I have never seen you look so happy before," she said.

48
00:03:43.749 --> 00:03:45.810
"Do you think so?"

49
00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:50.471
asked Grandfather with a smile, "Well, yes, Heidi.

50
00:03:51.071 --> 00:03:53.652
I am happier today than I thought was possible.

51
00:03:55.312 --> 00:03:58.295
I have been angry with the people of Dorfli for too long.

52
00:03:59.375 --> 00:04:02.017
It is good to be at peace with God and friends again."

53
00:04:02.978 --> 00:04:04.860
He put his arm around Heidi's shoulders.

54
00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:08.603
"God was good to me when he sent you to my hut."

55
00:04:09.063 --> 00:04:09.924
Grandfather said.
